Peak VRAM drops from 64.9~GB (vanilla) to 18.3~GB (L2C), 11.4~GB (FCLC), 7.0~GB (DPC) and 5.1~GB with TA-FJLT, i.e. 12.7$\times$ below vanilla and 27\% below DPC. Quality remains inside the $\delta=0.05$ budget: DiT-XL/2-$256^2$ $\Delta$FID $+0.018\pm0.006$; DiT-XL/2-$512^2$ $\Delta$FID $+0.031\pm0.008$; PixArt-Sigma-S $\Delta$FVD-16 $+0.27\pm0.18$. Extra FLOPs $+5.2\%$, latency $+1.7\%$ for images yet $-9.4\%$ for video due to larger batches. Energy per sample drops by 41\% relative to vanilla. The analytic $\sum_t \varepsilon_t$ explains 93\% of $\Delta$FID variance; empirical MSE exceeds $\varepsilon_t$ in only 3.1\% of steps and never violates the global $\delta$.  
